+    // pipelinedI2f (--fpu-i2f-pipelined): the int->float normalization
+    // (leading-zero count, then shift) runs in the lane's own stages instead
+    // of the shared unpacker side-pipeline, so fcvt.s.w[u] no longer freezes
+    // the lane.  The packer is fed three stages later from registered values;
+    // the arithmetic is the same expressions as the side-pipeline's.  (Kept
+    // below the original code so the default netlist stays byte-identical:
+    // SpinalHDL names some signals after source line numbers.)
+    val onCvtPiped = pipelinedI2f generate new Area {
+      val shiftWidth = log2Up(cvtWidth + 1)
+      val s0 = new layer.lane.Execute(unpackAt) {
